§§ `מקרי קצה`

-- The edge-case findings (MMS-534, MMS-552), asked of the root: inputs the
-- text did not picture, where the instruments part and the root rules.
-- Each holds while the instruments disagree; if one is brought into line,
-- it goes red and the finding is looked at again.

-- What each instrument that speaks says, by its name, and the ruling: what
-- an edge case's page shows.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `what each instrument says on` i c IS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD CONCAT x's `by`'s `title`, ": ", TOSTRING (x's `answer`)) (`the claims on` i c)

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the ruling shown on` i c IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i c
    WHEN JUST r THEN CONCAT TOSTRING (r's `the answer`), " — ", r's `governed by`'s `title`, " — ", r's `by the rule`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "אף מסמך אינו מדבר"

-- F-2025-26_tashpo_01-r: an owner's special-education teacher in 2025/26
-- mentoring 20 interns. The agreement of 19.3.2017 pays 2.4% "for each
-- intern" with no cap, 48% of the combined salary; the circular pays for
-- three at most, 7.2%. The agreement governs.
`a mentor of 20 interns` MEANS
    `a role holder` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) `employed by another owning body` `a recognised unofficial special-education school` 20 0
#EVAL `what each instrument says on` `the mentor's allowance rate` `a mentor of 20 interns`
#EVAL `the ruling shown on` `the mentor's allowance rate` `a mentor of 20 interns`
#ASSERT `the answers on` `the mentor's allowance rate` `a mentor of 20 interns` EQUALS LIST 0.48, 0.072
#ASSERT `the answer that governs` `the mentor's allowance rate` `a mentor of 20 interns` EQUALS JUST 0.48
-- How the root gets there, step by step: `l4 trace` draws it (GraphViz).
#EVALTRACE `the answer that governs` `the mentor's allowance rate` `a mentor of 20 interns`

-- F-2025-26_tashpo_01-t: an owner's special-education teacher in 2025/26
-- holding three roles, the district manager having approved the third. The
-- base agreement's §39(ב) pays three role allowances; the circular two,
-- approval or not. The agreement governs.
`a holder of three roles, the third approved` MEANS
    `a holder of roles` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) `employed by another owning body` `a recognised unofficial special-education school` 3 TRUE
#EVAL `what each instrument says on` `the role allowances counted` `a holder of three roles, the third approved`
#EVAL `the ruling shown on` `the role allowances counted` `a holder of three roles, the third approved`
#ASSERT `the answers on` `the role allowances counted` `a holder of three roles, the third approved` EQUALS LIST 3, 2
#ASSERT `the answer that governs` `the role allowances counted` `a holder of three roles, the third approved` EQUALS JUST 3

-- The same teacher without the approval: both pay two, and there is
-- nothing to resolve.
`a holder of three roles, none approved` MEANS
    `a holder of roles` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) `employed by another owning body` `a recognised unofficial special-education school` 3 FALSE
#ASSERT `the answers on` `the role allowances counted` `a holder of three roles, none approved` EQUALS LIST 2, 2
#ASSERT null (`the contradictions on` `the role allowances counted` `a holder of three roles, none approved`)
